struct Qdisc *q = tcf_block_q(tp->chain->block);
if (id && (TC_H_MAJ(id) == 0 || !(TC_H_MAJ(id ^ q->handle)))) {
Reason:
On shared blocks, `tcf_block_q()` returns NULL because there is no single Qdisc associated with the block. The old code immediately dereferences `q` to access `q->handle` without checking if `q` is NULL, causing a NULL pointer dereference when an old-style cls_fw filter is published to the datapath before its `->change()` function completes.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (tcf_block_shared(tp->chain->block))
    return -1;
q = tcf_block_q(tp->chain->block);
Reason:
Adding a check for shared blocks before accessing `q` ensures that when the block is shared, `fw_classify()` returns `-1` (fail classification) early, preventing the NULL dereference. Only after confirming the block is not shared is `q` safely assigned from `tcf_block_q()`.

